  "rulebook": {
    "assetTaxonomy": {},
    "assetCatalog": {
      "Ability§Blast 2": {
        "text": "Each time this weapon targets a unit, apply the 11th-edition **Blast 2** weapon ability."
      },
      "Ability§Ancestral Guidance": {
        "text": "At the start of your Command phase, select one stance. It remains active until the start of your next Command phase.\n\n**Ancestral Assault:** Improve the AP characteristic of attacks made by VEILED CONCORD models by 1.\n\n**Ancestral Bulwark:** Add 1 to Armour saving throws made for VEILED CONCORD models. This does not improve invulnerable saving throws."
      },
      "Ability§Recall": {
        "text": "Your army starts the battle with 0 Recall Points (RP), to a maximum of 13 RP.\n\nAt the start of your Command phase, gain 2 RP. Gain 1 additional RP if you control at least half of the objective markers in No Man's Land, rounding up, or control your opponent's home objective marker. Each time your army destroys an enemy unit, gain 1 RP.\n\nOnce per Command phase, you can spend 3 RP to gain 1CP, subject to the normal limit on gaining additional CP.\n\nIn your Command phase, you can perform any number of Recalls if you have sufficient RP and eligible Anchors. Select one destroyed VEILED CONCORD unit and one friendly VEILED CONCORD ANCHOR unit that has not already been selected as an Anchor this turn. Pay the destroyed unit's Recall cost. The Anchor becomes Channeling. At the end of the Command phase, return the destroyed unit at full Starting Strength, with all models at full wounds, within 6\" of that Anchor and more than 9\" horizontally from all enemy models.\n\nA returned unit can act normally that turn. It gains DAEMON and, if it lacks an equal or better invulnerable save, a 5+ invulnerable save. If it is not a CHARACTER, it loses ANCHOR for the rest of the battle. Losing ANCHOR does **not** prevent that unit from being Recalled again later; ANCHOR only determines whether a unit can channel a Recall.\n\n**Channeling:** Until the start of your next Command phase, a Channeling unit cannot make a Normal Move, Advance, Fall Back, shoot in your Shooting phase, or declare a charge. It can still fight, control objectives, use abilities and Stratagems, fire Overwatch, and make other out-of-phase attacks.\n\n**Attached Units:** For Recall, each constituent datasheet of an Attached unit is treated as a separate unit. Each destroyed constituent unit must be Recalled separately, and a returned unit does not automatically become Attached.\n\n**ANCHOR CLARIFICATION:** Losing ANCHOR only prevents a unit from being selected to channel future Recalls. It does not prevent that unit from being selected as the destroyed unit for Recall, and the same unit can be returned using Recall multiple times during a battle if you can pay its RP cost and have an eligible Anchor."
      },
