      "Enhancement§Twin-Soul Commander": {
        "text": "VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER model only. When forming a Link that includes the bearer’s unit, the two units can be within 9\" instead of 6\". Once those units are Linked, that Link is not broken if they later move farther apart during that phase.",
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Concord of Two Realms"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Points": {
            "value": 20
          }
        }
      },
      "Enhancement§Echo of the Other": {
        "text": "VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER model only. While the bearer’s unit is within 6\" of a friendly VEILED CONCORD unit of the opposite DAEMON status, add 1 to the bearer’s unit’s OC and it can re-roll Battle-shock tests. If both units are below Starting Strength, models in the bearer’s unit also have Feel No Pain 6+.",
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Concord of Two Realms"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Points": {
            "value": 15
          }
        }
      },
      "Enhancement§Concordant Instinct": {
        "text": "VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER model only. Once per phase, when the bearer’s Linked partner scores a Critical Hit or Critical Wound, the bearer’s unit gains both Souls in Concert bonuses until the end of that phase.",
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Concord of Two Realms"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Points": {
            "value": 25
          }
        }
      },
      "Enhancement§Bridge Between Worlds": {
        "text": "VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER model only. In your Command phase, select one friendly VEILED CONCORD unit of the opposite DAEMON status within 6\" of the bearer. Until the start of your next Command phase, both selected units can re-roll Advance and Charge rolls. Each time either selected unit destroys an enemy unit, add 1 to the other selected unit’s OC until the start of your next Command phase.",
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Concord of Two Realms"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Points": {
            "value": 15
          }
        }
      },
      "Stratagem§Expand the Boundary": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sovereign Dominion"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Command"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your Command phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One objective marker you control.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the start of your next Command phase, that objective marker and the area within 6\" horizontally of it are within your Dominion."
      },
      "Stratagem§Sanctuary's Aegis": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sovereign Dominion"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Shooting",
            "Fight"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your opponent's Shooting phase or the Fight phase, just after an enemy selects a friendly unit within your Dominion as a target.\n\n**TARGET:** That friendly VEILED CONCORD unit.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the attacking unit finishes making its attacks, models in your unit have a 5+ invulnerable save. If they already have an invulnerable save, improve it by 1 to a maximum of 4+. If your unit is also within range of an objective marker you control, models in it also have Feel No Pain 6+ against those attacks."
      },
      "Stratagem§The King's Ground": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sovereign Dominion"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Movement"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Start of your opponent's Movement phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One enemy unit within your Dominion.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the end of the turn, subtract 2\" from its Move characteristic and subtract 2 from Advance and Charge rolls made for it. It cannot receive bonuses to those values. If it is within range of an objective marker you control, it cannot Fall Back unless it passes a Leadership test."
      },
      "Stratagem§Judgement Within the Veil": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sovereign Dominion"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Shooting",
            "Fight"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your Shooting phase or the Fight phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD unit and one enemy unit within your Dominion.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the end of the phase, add 1 to Wound rolls made by your unit against that enemy and those attacks have [IGNORES COVER]. If the enemy is also within range of an objective marker, improve the AP characteristic of those attacks by 1."
      },
      "Stratagem§The Realm Answers": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sovereign Dominion"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Movement"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your opponent's Movement phase, just after an enemy unit ends a Normal Move, Advance or Fall Back within your Dominion.\n\n**TARGET:** One friendly VEILED CONCORD unit within 9\" of that enemy unit.\n\n**EFFECT:** Your unit can make a Normal Move of D6+2\", but cannot end within Engagement Range. If it ends that move within range of an objective marker, add 1 to its OC until the end of the turn."
      },
      "Stratagem§Walk the Sovereign Paths": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sovereign Dominion"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Movement"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** End of your Movement phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One non-TITANIC VEILED CONCORD unit wholly within your Dominion and not within Engagement Range.\n\n**EFFECT:** Determine the boundaries of your Dominion before removing the selected unit. Remove it from the battlefield and set it back up wholly within an area that was within your Dominion when this Stratagem was used and more than 9\" horizontally from all enemy models. It counts as having made a Normal Move."
      },
      "Detachment§Sovereign Dominion": {
        "stats": {
          "Detachment Points": {
            "value": 3
          }
        },
        "text": "**SOVEREIGN DOMINION**\n\nYour deployment zone is always within your Dominion. If there is at least one objective marker in No Man’s Land and you control at least half of those objective markers, rounding up, No Man’s Land is within your Dominion. If there is at least one objective marker in your opponent’s deployment zone and you control at least half of those objective markers, rounding up, that deployment zone is within your Dominion. In addition, the area within 6\" of each friendly VEILED CONCORD PSYKER model is always within your Dominion.\n\n**SANCTUARY RESTORATION:** At the end of your Command phase, each friendly VEILED CONCORD unit within your Dominion can restore one wounded model by D3 lost wounds. If a friendly DAEMON unit within your Dominion has no wounded models but is below Starting Strength, instead return one destroyed non-CHARACTER model to that unit with D3 wounds remaining, not exceeding its Wounds characteristic.\n\n**SANCTUARY SHELTER:** Subtract 1 from Hit rolls for ranged attacks that target friendly VEILED CONCORD units within your Dominion.\n\n**WEIGHT OF THE VEIL:** While an enemy unit is within your Dominion, worsen the AP characteristic of attacks made by models in that enemy unit by 1, to a minimum of AP0.",
        "rules": {
