          }
        }
      },
      "Stratagem§Countermand and Reissue": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Edicts of Command"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Any"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours",
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Start of any phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD unit currently affected by an Imperative.\n\n**EFFECT:** Replace its current Imperative with a different Imperative. If the unit is within 9\" of a friendly VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER, it can instead retain its current Imperative and gain one different Imperative until the end of the phase; this is an exception to the normal restriction that a unit can only be affected by one Imperative."
      },
      "Stratagem§No Hesitation": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Edicts of Command"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Movement"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your Movement phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD unit affected by the Advance Imperative.\n\n**EFFECT:** Instead of rolling to Advance, add 6\" to the unit’s Move characteristic for that Advance. It is eligible to shoot and charge in a turn in which it Advanced."
      },
      "Stratagem§Eliminate the Priority Target": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Edicts of Command"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Shooting",
            "Fight"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your Shooting phase or the Fight phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD unit affected by the Engage Imperative.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the end of the phase, unmodified Hit rolls of 5+ are Critical Hits and re-roll Wound rolls of 1. Against CHARACTER, MONSTER or VEHICLE units, also improve the AP characteristic of those attacks by 1."
      },
      "Stratagem§Hold at All Costs": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Edicts of Command"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Shooting",
            "Fight"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your opponent's Shooting phase or the Fight phase, just after an enemy selects a VEILED CONCORD unit affected by the Endure Imperative as a target.\n\n**TARGET:** That unit.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the attacking unit finishes making its attacks, models in your unit have Feel No Pain 5+ against attacks with a Damage characteristic of 2 or more. Enemy rules cannot worsen your unit’s Toughness or Save characteristics during those attacks."
      },
      "Stratagem§Claim in the King's Name": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Edicts of Command"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Command"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** End of your Command phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD unit affected by the Secure Imperative and within range of an objective marker.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the start of your next Command phase, double that unit’s OC. That objective remains under your control until your opponent controls it at the end of a phase. While enemy units are within range of that objective, their OC cannot be increased by abilities."
      },
      "Stratagem§Absolute Command": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Edicts of Command"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Any"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours",
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 2
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Start of any phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD unit within 12\" of a friendly VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the start of your next Command phase, the target unit benefits from all four Imperatives simultaneously.\n\n**RESTRICTIONS:** Once per battle round."
      },
      "Detachment§Edicts of Command": {
        "stats": {
          "Detachment Points": {
            "value": 2
          }
        },
        "text": "**IMPERATIVE NETWORK**\n\nIn your Command phase, each friendly VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER can select one friendly VEILED CONCORD unit within 9\"; an EPIC HERO can select up to two instead. A CHARACTER can select the unit it is leading. A unit can normally be affected by only one Imperative at a time. The selected Imperative lasts until the start of your next Command phase.\n\n**Advance:** Add 2\" to the unit’s Move characteristic and ranged weapons equipped by models in it gain [ASSAULT].\n\n**Engage:** Add 1 to Hit rolls made by models in the unit.\n\n**Endure:** Each time an attack with Damage 2 or more is allocated to a model in the unit, subtract 1 from that attack’s Damage, to a minimum of 1.\n\n**Secure:** Add 2 to the unit’s OC and it automatically passes Battle-shock tests.",
        "rules": {
