      "Enhancement§Voice of the King": {
        "text": "VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER model only. In your Command phase, the bearer can select one additional friendly unit for Imperative Network. Once per battle round, one unit selected by the bearer can receive two different Imperatives simultaneously until the start of your next Command phase.",
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Edicts of Command"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Points": {
            "value": 30
          }
        }
      },
      "Enhancement§Grand Strategist": {
        "text": "VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER model only. After both players have deployed their armies, you can redeploy up to two VEILED CONCORD units. When doing so, those units can be placed into Strategic Reserves regardless of the normal limit.",
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Edicts of Command"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Points": {
            "value": 20
          }
        }
      },
      "Enhancement§Command Nexus": {
        "text": "VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER model only. Increase the bearer’s Imperative Network range to 15\". In addition, the bearer can issue an Imperative through one friendly VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER within 12\"; when it does, measure the selection range from either the bearer or that CHARACTER.",
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Edicts of Command"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Points": {
            "value": 20
          }
        }
      },
      "Enhancement§Master of Contingencies": {
        "text": "VEILED CONCORD CHARACTER model only. Once per battle round, at the start of any phase, select one friendly VEILED CONCORD unit within 9\" that is currently affected by an Imperative. Replace that Imperative with another. If the selected unit is the bearer’s own unit, it can instead retain its current Imperative and gain the new one until the end of the phase.",
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Edicts of Command"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Points": {
            "value": 20
          }
        }
      },
      "Stratagem§Lock Shields": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sanctum Phalanx"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Shooting",
            "Fight"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your opponent's Shooting phase or the Fight phase, just after an enemy selects a VEILED CONCORD INFANTRY unit as a target.\n\n**TARGET:** That INFANTRY unit.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the attacking unit finishes making its attacks, worsen the AP characteristic of those attacks by 1, to a minimum of AP0. If your unit is SANCTUM CATAPHRACTS and an attack’s Strength is greater than its Toughness, also subtract 1 from the Wound roll."
      },
      "Stratagem§Advance of the Phalanx": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sanctum Phalanx"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Movement"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your Movement phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD INFANTRY unit.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the end of the turn, add 2\" to its Move characteristic and ranged weapons equipped by models in it gain [ASSAULT]. If it is SANCTUM CATAPHRACTS, add 3\" instead and it counts as having Remained Stationary for the purposes of the Sanctum Phalanx Detachment rule until the start of your next Movement phase."
      },
      "Stratagem§Crush the Breach": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sanctum Phalanx"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Fight"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours",
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Fight phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD INFANTRY unit.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the end of the phase, add 1 to melee Wound rolls made by models in your unit. If it is SANCTUM CATAPHRACTS, also improve the AP characteristic of its melee attacks by 1 and those attacks gain [LETHAL HITS] against enemy units within range of an objective marker."
      },
      "Stratagem§Unbroken Firing Line": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sanctum Phalanx"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Shooting"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Your Shooting phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD INFANTRY unit.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the end of the phase, ranged attacks made by models in your unit have [IGNORES COVER] and re-roll Hit rolls of 1. If it is SANCTUM CATAPHRACTS, also re-roll Wound rolls of 1."
      },
      "Stratagem§Stand Where They Fell": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sanctum Phalanx"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Any"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Yours",
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** End of any phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD INFANTRY unit that lost one or more models this phase.\n\n**EFFECT:** Return one destroyed non-CHARACTER model to the unit with 1 wound remaining. If the unit is SANCTUM CATAPHRACTS, return that model with 2 wounds remaining instead.\n\n**RESTRICTIONS:** Each unit can only be targeted by this Stratagem once per battle."
      },
      "Stratagem§None Shall Pass": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Veiled Concord",
            "Sanctum Phalanx"
          ],
          "Category": [
            "Strategic Ploy"
          ],
          "Phase": [
            "Charge"
          ],
          "Turn": [
            "Opponent’s"
          ]
        },
        "stats": {
          "Command Cost": {
            "value": 2
          }
        },
        "text": "**WHEN:** Start of your opponent's Charge phase.\n\n**TARGET:** One VEILED CONCORD INFANTRY unit.\n\n**EFFECT:** Until the end of the phase, subtract 2 from Charge rolls made by enemy units that declare your unit as a target. If an enemy unit completes a charge against your unit, add 1 to melee Hit rolls made by your unit against that enemy until the end of the turn. If your unit is SANCTUM CATAPHRACTS, each time an enemy unit declares a charge against it, your unit can fire Overwatch against that enemy even if it has already fired Overwatch this phase, without spending additional CP; those Overwatch attacks hit on unmodified Hit rolls of 4+."
      },
      "Detachment§Sanctum Phalanx": {
        "stats": {
          "Detachment Points": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "**SANCTUM PHALANX**\n\nIf a friendly SANCTUM CATAPHRACTS unit Remained Stationary in your previous Movement phase, until the start of your next Movement phase add 1 to the OC characteristic of models in that unit and re-roll saving throws of 1 made for models in that unit.\n\nIn addition, friendly SANCTUM CATAPHRACTS units can be targeted with the Fire Overwatch Stratagem for 0CP, and when resolving those Overwatch attacks, unmodified Hit rolls of 4+ score hits.",
        "rules": {
